NAME
     ls - list directory contents

SYNOPSIS
     ls [-a] [-l] [-h] [-R] [-i] [-d] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     For each FILE, ls writes its name; for a directory, the names of
     the things inside it. With no FILE it lists the working directory.
     Names beginning with a dot are left out unless -a is given.

OPTIONS
     -a   include names beginning with a dot
     -l   one line per name: type and mode, links, owner, group, size,
          time of last change, and the name
     -h   with -l, sizes in kilobytes and megabytes rather than bytes
     -R   descend into directories
     -i   print each name's inode number
     -d   list a directory itself rather than what is in it

SEE ALSO
     stat(1), find(1), du(1)
